# Buyer Founder — project memory

Marketing site for the solo-founder catalog. Next.js on port 3400.

## What is actually usable from this site

- `/try` — in-browser PainFork wizard. Uses vendored `@painfork/core` at `vendor/painfork-core` (snapshot of PainFork's browser entry). Import `/browser`, never the Node session (`fs`).
- `/waitlist` — email capture. `POST /api/waitlist` writes to Supabase `waitlist_signups` when `SUPABASE_URL` + `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` are set; otherwise appends to `data/waitlist.jsonl` locally (gitignored). No public read of emails.
- `/l/[slug]` — campaign landings (minimal nav). Config in `src/lib/campaigns.ts`.
- `/pain/[slug]` — SEO pain-intent pages. Config in `src/lib/pain-pages.ts`.
- Analytics: `@vercel/analytics` + optional GA/Meta via `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` env vars. Events: `waitlist_signup`, `try_example_loaded`, `try_wedge_exported`, `sample_view`, `campaign_view`.
- UTM params (`utm_source`, `utm_medium`, `utm_campaign`) stored in cookies (`bf_utm_*`) and attached to waitlist signups.
- `/samples/wedge` — PainFork one-pager generated from the shipped AS/400 example.
- `/samples/feasibility` — excerpt of the Feasibility Validator demo scan of fullstack-assistant (overall 73, verdict fix-first).
- `/samples/clauses` — Oak Hollow HOA sample in Clause Finder’s US checklist shape. Not legal advice.
- Planroom remains the only separately hosted app: `https://planroom-seven.vercel.app`.

## Do not

- Advertise all 14 SKUs as live.
- Send waitlist emails to mailto as the primary capture.
- Import `@painfork/core` (root) from client components — it pulls Node `fs`.
